{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Noah built an altar to YHWH.</b> Noah intended in his offerings the order of ascent from below upward: the altar first, and from there to the attribute of mercy — this is what it says, 'to YHWH' — and from mercy all is elevated and attributed to the supreme degree, which is the Cause of causes, blessed be He, and this is what it says, ״ויעל עולות במזבח״ — 'and he offered burnt-offerings on the altar' — it is written עלת (an ascent). And so the prophet said (Isaiah 60:7): ״יעלו לרצון על מזבחי ובית תפארתי אפאר״. And likewise with Manoah, we do not find that he built an altar, but he first made mention concerning the altar and afterward of heaven, and from there to the supreme degree, which is עלה, and then the influx returns: from above to mercy, and from mercy to the altar, which is called לב (heart), and from it to the supernal beings and to the lower beings. And this is what it says: ״וירח ה׳ את ריח הניחח״ — 'And YHWH smelled the pleasing fragrance' — that is, He drew down the drawing of the influx that descends from the Cause of causes; and then He said to His heart, ״לא אוסיף״ — 'I will not again' — that is, 'I will not give addition to the attribute of judgment to curse the earth because of man.' And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:20.033778581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}